From b7517c680d8fb7b29e5926d7739809e1215131b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:23:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 123/144] media: qcom: integrate SM8750 PHY and AON clock
 ownership

Use the SM8750 OEM two-phase lane sequence rather than the X1E fallback values. Hold the front camera CSI/MCLK ownership while its clock is prepared and restore the previous mux bits on release. Split the SoC PHY resources from CAMSS and retain the initial three-RDI subset within the existing generic pad API.

Link: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oneplus_sm8750/tree/d50b305f7da9e14715a25120a4ac7b1a4b8b97c3/vendor/qcom/opensource/camera-kernel/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_csiphy

